--- body ---
## Context
Raid 2026-10-27, author ruling. The raid hand-rolled the same landing command for each of 12 merges:
pin the ruled head, `merge-gate.py check`, `run` and `check` again when main moved (twice today a
peer merge staled the record mid-run), disarm auto-merge, `gh pr merge --match-head-commit`, read
back, log a timing row. Each hand-roll is an orchestrator turn and a chance to slip (a session-id
placeholder went out unfilled once today). The merge recipe stays the single contract; this script
executes it.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One call per PR: verifies the head equals the gate's ruled tip, runs `/merge`'s steps 1 and 3-8
      (close when claimed, check/record with one retry on a moved base, disarm, pinned merge,
      read-back), and prints one `<pr> merge <start> <end>` row for `step_clock.py`.
- [ ] Refuses (non-zero, reason printed) on head drift, a failing record, a second stale record or
      an unreadable read-back; never re-runs a merge.
- [ ] Forge calls sit behind one adapter, so ticket 1252's no-forge path can plug in.
- [ ] raid Phase 7 calls it; `skills/merge/SKILL.md` stays the contract it cites.
- [ ] Tests on a temp repo with a stubbed forge; the harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
skills/merge/SKILL.md, skills/raid/SKILL.md, scripts/merge-gate.py, new scripts/raid_land.py

